- role: assistant
  content: |
    Root cause and fix
    - Cause: FastAPI was redirecting /api/users → /api/users/ with a 307 and an absolute Location header without the port, because Nginx forwarded Host as $host (no port). The browser then followed the redirect to http://localhost/api/users/ (port 80), causing “Failed to fetch”.
    - Fix applied: In Nginx, preserve the original port and forward proxy headers.
      - Set Host to $http_host and add X-Forwarded-Host/Proto.
      - Also added listen [::]:80 for IPv6.
      - File: infra/nginx/conf/default.conf
    - Result: Redirects now include the port (http://localhost:8080/api/users/), so the Users page loads correctly.

    What to do now
    - Hard refresh the browser on Users (or open a new incognito window). The list should load. Creating users should also work.

    Unstaged changes and whether they make sense
    - backend/ddms/db/models.py
      - Persist Enum using lowercase values (owner/admin/viewer) via values_callable to match the migration and avoid enum insert errors. Keep it.
    - docker-compose.yml
      - Healthcheck path updated to /api/health to match our routes. Keep it.
    - infra/nginx/conf/default.conf
      - Use $http_host and forwarded headers, plus IPv6 listen. Keep it.

    If you confirm the Users page now works, I’ll commit these changes. Feel free to suggest your preferred single or split commit titles; here are concise options with no “Why” lines:
    - 10.5-fix(proxy): preserve port in Host; add forwarded headers
    - 10.6-fix(db): enum mapping to lowercase values
    - 10.7-fix(compose): backend healthcheck to /api/health
